  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025 Philippine Election Observation Mission</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will support an independent international observation mission to the 2025 Philippine Midterm Elections. The 2025 elections are critical for the Philippines. The introduction of new reforms, from new automated counting machines to implementation of online voting bring potential challenges to election integrity and inclusivity. The observation mission will focus on three things: (a) Political context and campaign environment; (b) Implementation of technological advancements; and (c) social media and disinformation. It will deploy a number of long term observers across the country who will conduct pre-election, Election Day and post-election activities. The mission will also assess the impact of social media on electoral integrity, alongside COMELEC regulations on candidates&apos; online activities. The mission will particularly be useful in monitoring developments in Southern Philippines, as the Bangsamoro region transitions from an interim government to an elected parliamentary system as part of the peace process.</narrative>
  </description>
